# Lessons learned (don't relearn the hard way)

When you figure out a tricky, non-obvious **technical** problem (races, cache,
network, blocking, correctness), **append a short entry below** so it isn’t lost.
Skip obvious UI polish (colors, icon choice, spacing, copy). Format each as
**symptom → cause → fix** in 1–3 lines. Newest first. Keep it tight; prune duplicates.

## Lessons

- **TTS rest stole another utterance's quota.** Follow-up Redis key was
  `user_id` only, so a second speak's `rest` consumed the first lead's
  unbilled budget. Store `clips:chars:lead_hash`; rest must send that hash
  or it is billed. Speaker does not need the mic; cloud 502 falls back to
  `expo-speech` (not API-down).
- **SSE New chat aborted the in-flight reply.** SSE has no `cancel` message —
  Stop *is* abort (close the fetch). New chat / leave must not `abort()`; latch
  `chatId` so leftover events cannot paint the next thread. Register the SSE
  producer with `register_inflight_stream` so `GET /messages` can wait like WS.
- **Live talk abort skipped refund.** `body_iter` refunded in `except Exception`;
  abort is `CancelledError` / `GeneratorExit`. Settle in `finally`: no audio →
  refund; audio → clear pending + persist. Unsupported containers fail closed
  (no Whisper+TTS echo). Client abort before the first `audio` event hits
  `POST /live/refund`.
- **Live talk waited 20s and left no chat.** `/speech/live/speak` drained the
  full OpenRouter SSE, wrapped one WAV, then JSON; the client ignored
  `transcript`. Stream WAV clips as PCM arrives, Whisper the user in
  parallel, persist both sides as chat rows, play clips as they land.
- **Live talk hid the chat hamburger.** Full-screen `Modal` is a new window, so
  ChatHeader under it cannot open the drawer. In-tree overlay with `top:
  headerInset` and `bottom: composerClearance` (0 header inset while the
  drawer is open) so type/attach still work. Mute is the mic next to close
  (red = model cannot hear); not the orb.
- **Gallery `GET /attachments/{id}/file` 404 after a reboot.** List 200s from Neon, then each thumb 404s. Cause: local backend defaulted to `/tmp/recall-attachments`; macOS wipes `/tmp`, rows stay. Fix: store under `~/.recall/attachments` (`expanduser`); omit local rows whose blob is gone from the gallery list; log `attachment blob missing on disk` on `/file`.
- **Repeat on New reminder did nothing.** Nested `AppSheet` is a second RN
  `Modal`; iOS will not present it over the add-reminder sheet. Put the
  pick-one list in the same sheet (expand in place).
- **Library always skeletoned after Back.** `useGalleryData` stored lastFetchAt in
  the hook, so leaving `/gallery` dropped the 20s skip. Use a module
  `StaleResourceCache` (hydrate + drawer prefetch All); invalidate on logout,
  chat delete, upload, and image-gen. Keep per-tab snapshots so filter switches
  do not paint the previous tab. Drop a 404 thumb from the list in-session.
- **Chat ⋮ Share icon did nothing (no Messages/Mail sheet).** `onShareFromMenu` called
  `closeMenu()` then `Share.share`. AppSheet is an RN `Modal`; presenting the OS
  activity sheet on a dismissing modal makes iOS drop it. Keep the sheet up until
  `Share.share` returns, then close. Don't swallow share errors except user cancel
  (`did not share` / cancel / dismiss).
- **Isolate-x step showed raw `1\cdot x = 2 - 3^{\frac{2}{3}}`; `3^{2/3}` looked like `32/3`.**
  Model `$`-wrapped the bullet (`$- 1\cdot x = …$`); prose-bullet unwrap stripped
  dollars after command-wrap had skipped the interior, so `\cdot`/`\frac` never
  reached MathText. Keep `$…$` when the inner span is math. Wrapping only
  `\frac` also shattered `3^{$\frac{2}{3}$}`. Wrap the whole island. `toSuperscript("2/3")`
  was null so styles.sup sat at baseline next to `3` — map `2/3` → `²⁄³`.
- **Chart / bare email interviewed; coffee mermaid parse-failed.** `CLARIFICATION_HINT`
  is on every non-quiz turn and fought the layout hints: no rainfall numbers or a
  bare `escribeme un correo` became 1–3 questions instead of ` ```chart ` /
  ` ```email `. Chart/email/flowchart exceptions draft immediately. Unquoted
  `E[Grind Beans (Medium Grind)]` is invalid Mermaid — quote labels in the hint
  and run a linear sanitizer on persist + `MermaidBlock`.
- **Famous quote rendered as italic `"…" - Author` prose.** Slim turns get
  `COMPACT_RESPONSE_FORMAT_HINT` (plain prose) and QuoteBlock only fires on
  markdown `>` blockquotes. Swap compact for `QUOTE_FORMAT_HINT`; promote
  wrapped `"quote" - Author` paragraphs; split same-line ` — Name` (space
  before the dash). Even hairline — no left stripe. Never ` ```quote `.
- **4-week Spanish plan became a clipped 3-column table.** FORMAT_CONTRACT
  allows pipe tables for "schedules," so a learning plan looked like a grid.
  `HOWTO_FORMAT_HINT` wins on N-week/roadmap/how-do-I asks: `##` + lists, never
  a table. Say timetable, not schedule, for real grids.
- **Study tips were a jokey essay, no Tip/Warning cards.** Slim turns get
  `COMPACT_RESPONSE_FORMAT_HINT` (plain prose) and never see FORMAT_CONTRACT's
  callout line, so "include a warning" became `## A Friendly Warning`. Swap
  compact for `CALLOUT_FORMAT_HINT` (`> Tip:` / `> Warning:` blockquotes).
- **Chart leftover `3.1` pill + expand did nothing.** After overflow-clip, the
  gray centered `3.1` was still the rainfall *mean* as `looksLikeMathAnswer` →
  AnswerBlock (empty-lang / ```answer after the fence), not Vega paint. Strip
  that bare-number crumb after chart fences. Expand used already-clamped
  `heightRef`, so toggle was a no-op; keep raw `reportedHeight` and hide the
  control unless the SVG is clipped.
- **Email card showed `[Manager's Name]` / `[Your Name]`.** The copy hint already banned
  placeholders, but models still emit `To: [Manager's Email Address]`. Drop those
  form-slots in `parseEmailDraft` (omit To, greet `Hi,`, strip from subject) so
  copy/Gmail are send-ready even when the model ignores the hint.
- **“Near me” asked for a city instead of the OS location sheet.** An in-app
  “Turn on Location” Alert sat in front of `requestForegroundPermissionsAsync`,
  so the system prompt never appeared and the LLM interviewed for a neighborhood.
  Geo asks go straight to the OS sheet; Expo Go alerts and does not send.
- **Right triangle 3-4-5 became 6x4 with a gray `12` pill.** `first_dim_pair`
  only sees `8 x 5` / `by`, so "legs 3 and 4" missed and the draw default
  (base=6, height=4) shipped — area 12 as ```answer. Parse two numbers after
  `legs`; skip the area pill unless they asked for area. Pad the SVG so the
  base length label is not clipped.
- **Chart vs ChatGPT: months clipped, stray “3.1”, thumbs gone.** Vega
  `height` is the inner plot, so x-axis labels (and a tick/tooltip) painted
  *below* the 350px WebView onto the action row. Prefer horizontal bars
  (category on y), size the WebView to the SVG bbox, `overflow: hidden`,
  `tooltip: false`.
- **Bar chart months came out Apr, Feb, Jan… with a device-tall white card.**
  Vega-Lite alphabetizes nominal x unless `sort` is null; the preview body used
  `min-height: 100vh`, so the WebView ate the screen and the scroll-to-bottom
  chevron sat on the last prose line. Normalize `encoding.x.sort = null` before
  embed; drop the 100vh body. Prompt: listed order + stop after the fence.
- **Chart card showed a CSP eval error instead of bars.** Vega compiles
  filter/calc expressions with `new Function()`. Default preview CSP is
  `script-src 'unsafe-inline'` only, so the WebView painted "Refused to
  evaluate a string as JavaScript". Use `CHART_PREVIEW_CSP` (`unsafe-eval`)
  on that document only — keep eval off user-HTML `PREVIEW_CSP`.
- **Coffee mermaid was a jokey 2-node card, clipped at 220px.** Slim turns
  get `COMPACT_RESPONSE_FORMAT_HINT` (plain prose) and no mermaid layout, so
  the model invents a bit instead of the requested steps. Swap compact for
  `MERMAID_FORMAT_HINT` on flowchart asks. The WebView was a fixed 220px with
  scroll off — size to the SVG via `mermaid-size` postMessage (cap 640).
- **Bar chart became a joke + markdown table (or broken Mermaid).** Slim
  turns get `COMPACT_RESPONSE_FORMAT_HINT` and no ```chart example, so
  "make a bar chart" claims it cannot draw and dumps a rainfall table —
  or, after a mermaid thread, `graph TDJan: 5.7in`. Swap compact for
  `CHART_FORMAT_HINT` (Vega-Lite ```chart; you CAN draw; never a table).
- **Compare Python vs Java was a wall of text, no code cards.** Slim/casual
  turns inject `COMPACT_RESPONSE_FORMAT_HINT` (plain prose, no `##` headings).
  `FORMAT_CONTRACT` only lands on rich turns, and `COMPARISON_FORMAT_HINT` was
  never appended. On vs/compare queries, swap compact for that hint (table,
  then `###` + tagged fences as code cards). Tone guard must not ban leading
  with that table.
- **Comparison table inside a python code block + no horizontal pan.**
  `breakAttachedMathFences` lifted `| … | ```python` onto its own line; the
  closer (` ``` | ```java`) never matched, so the next GFM table was fence
  body. Don't detach fences from table rows; split a swallowed `| --- |`
  table back out of ` ```python `. A ScrollView that grows to content width
  cannot pan — lock the viewport to the bubble, hide the indicator (no
  purple overflow strip). Prompt: short prose cells; code under ### after.
- **Inline `\frac` numerators vanished over the line above.** iOS sizes a
  stacked-frac View inside markdown `Text` as 0×0, so the numerator paints on
  the previous sentence. Host those runs in a row-wrap View (`md-math-inline-wrap`);
  keep `mathRunLineHeight` at MATH_TALL (46) for any `\frac`/`\sqrt` — shrinking
  to 34 when the paragraph was long clipped the 40px stack. Real vinculum
  (num / bar / den), not `¹─₂` / `½`.
- **Web GFM tables vanished.** marked parsed pipe tables, then DOMPurify
  `ALLOWED_TAGS` omitted `table`/`img` so the cells disappeared. Allow table tags
  and `img`; replace JSON rich fences with a short label before parse.
- **Settled assistant showed chain-of-thought.** `ReasoningBlock` rendered live
  CoT and kept `reasoning_preview` after `done`. Status/waiting is enough; do not
  copy reasoning onto `Message` (second door, same class as recalled-memory chips).
- **user_quota still ~1s after persist left the first-token path.** Every
  send ran `COUNT(*)` plus a Redis usage EXISTS while holding a Neon
  checkout. Use `len(recent)` when the window is not full; only COUNT when
  it is (older rows may exist). Check the Redis usage key before opening
  Neon so a warm day does not pin a connection on EXISTS.
- **Lightweight send still waited ~650ms after prompt was ready.** Persist
  overlapped prompt assembly, but gather waited for the Neon commit before
  LiteLLM. Start the model as soon as the prompt is ready; await the user-row
  task before finalize so the assistant cannot commit first.
- **Send still hesitated ~4s after the 10s self-wait.** Persist (Neon insert)
  then prompt `list_recent` / `has_chunks` ran in series, and Pro revision
  intercept re-fetched the same recent window. Load user+chat+recent+mode in
  one session; overlap persist with prompt; skip the chunk probe unless this
  turn has files, recent rows show `[File:`/`[Image:`, or the thread is at
  the recent-window cap.
- **`$x^{6}=1$` waited ~30s then "model isn't responding".** Composer
  `$` / `x^{6}` failed the ASCII equation walker, so heuristic SymPy
  missed and the tool loop ran non-streaming `complete_with_tools` on
  R1 (smart-chat). Unwrap `$`/`^{n}` in latex normalize; tool selection
  uses the fast alias; timeout is a warning + stream, not a traceback.
- **Drawer titles copied the first user line (`hi`).** `firstReplyTitlePlan`
  stamped that as the title and skipped GET poll, so the topic job never
  reached the sidebar. Insert untitled (Image/File overlay only) and poll;
  keep patching the left-behind row after New chat. Greetings store
  `Greeting`, not the opener.
- **New chat mid-stream stopped the reply.** Pencil sent WS `cancel` and
  disconnect cancelled the producer, so the left-behind thread only kept a
  truncated bubble. New chat must not stop; disconnect drains the model
  stream and persists the full assistant. Stop still cancels. Only DELETE
  (`force`) stops on leave.
- **New chat mid-stream vanished from the drawer.** Pencil closes the per-chat
  WS before `done`, and `handleFirstReply` (insert row) only ran on `done`.
  Empty-check also deleted user-only threads. Insert the row from the first
  user line before leaving; only DELETE unused empty drafts; WS disconnect
  awaits finalize like SSE.
- **First chat send waited 8s on a silent proxy.** WebSocket connect had no
  TCP reject, so `CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS` (8000) blocked SSE. Typing already showed;
  first token did not. Fall back at 1.5s and latch SSE — do not dual-stream.
- **Wi-Fi “connected” hid API-down and captive portals.** NetInfo `isConnected === true`
  skipped probes so a sticky iOS `isInternetReachable` would not pin the offline banner.
  Keep that immediate “not no-internet” path, but always probe: API up → online; public
  204 only → `api_unreachable`; both fail → `no_internet`. Do not treat connected as offline.
- **STT silence returned 502.** Whisper `text: ""` was coerced to `None`, and
  the router treated every None as a Bad Gateway. Return `""` for no-speech;
  502 only on HTTP/provider failure. Mobile already maps empty to
  `chat.voice_transcribe_empty`.
- **Home overdue card only after logout.** `overduePresented` hid the card after
  first paint; leaving Home remounted with an empty session set, so it vanished
  until logout wiped the nudge file. Hide only on dismiss (X) or complete.
- **Chat-extract deletes from Gmail/OCR text.** `build_todo_sync_transcript`
  used raw assistant/user bodies, including UNTRUSTED and `[Image:]` excerpts.
  Strip those blocks (linear scan) and cap deletes per turn.
- **Chat delete left billed R2 objects.** Rows committed, then `delete_bytes`
  failures were discarded — GDPR wipe cannot see key-only orphans. Detach
  `commit=False`, commit chat, enqueue failed keys for the reaper.
- **Quiz try counter reset after a second hint.** `find_original_quiz_fence_created_at`
  broke on the first earlier fence, and `list_recent_assistants` is newest-first,
  so it found the previous re-emit not the original. Scan all matches; take min
  `created_at`.
- **Same Gmail suggestion re-pushed every 60s.** `_push_cycle` collects on
  session A, then finalize mutates those ORM rows on session B. Writes look
  fine (`expire_on_commit=False`) but no UPDATE flushes. `session.get` the
  row on the finalize session. Single-session `run_push_cycle` tests miss this.
- **Metro: `messagesRef` already declared.** Rebase of stacked chat-loader
  PRs kept both `useRef(messages)` blocks. One ref at the top of the hook;
  later code only reads `.current`.
- **“Create music” rendered a chemistry molecule.** Default rich-turn
  hints taught ```smiles / ```tip / ```steps, and settled render ran
  `looksLikeMathAnswer` before explicit code langs. One Markdown
  `FORMAT_CONTRACT`; chemistry protocol only with chem context; one
  `classifyFence` (tagged lang wins). Keep old fence renderers for
  stored messages.
- **Attach send spun in the composer and the thread.** Optimistic bubble
  landed first, but the chip + `attachBusy` + `sendPhase` stayed until
  upload finished. Clear the chip immediately. Do not treat
  `pendingOutboundId` as "Sending" — show typing once the placeholder
  mounts, not after socket `start`.
- **Attach/upload photo polled `GET /chats/{id}` five times.** Image-only
  send has empty user text (`defaultAttachmentPrompt` is `""`), so the
  Home-chip provisional title was null and the topic poll still ran. Use
  "Image" / "File" as a local overlay; still poll until the topic job lands.
- **Back from Learning / Reminders still hit `GET /home`.** #1005 skipped
  Home only while a thread was open, so empty Home refetched after the
  20s window went stale. Skip if login already fetched Home.
- **First assistant bubble sat above the composer.** FlashList
  `startRenderingFromBottom` plus keyboard/`scrollToEnd` pin a short
  thread to the bottom. First turn (1–2 messages) renders from the top;
  skip `scrollToEnd` when content still fits (`maxOffset === 0`).
- **Pencil New chat hit `GET /home` and `GET …/messages?limit=20`.** Skipping
  Home while a thread is open lets the 20s cache go stale, so New chat
  refetched. Skip if login already fetched Home. Empty-probe ran because
  `startNewChat` clears messages before the route effect — remember chats
  that already had an assistant.
- **Lists / Learning / Reminders back reloaded the open thread.** Focus
  silent-refetched `GET …/messages` (20s TTL still fired). Do not refetch
  on in-app Back; App resume still recovers a truncated stream. Skip Home
  when a thread is open; reuse the message cache + drawer row on remount.
- **Help-me-think from Home still hit `/suggestions`, title poll, and TTS.**
  First reply reused `POST /chats` for the drawer row, then still fetched
  chips (job not ready) and warmed speak. Skip those; keep title poll or
  the drawer stays Untitled until pull-to-refresh. Speak loads on tap.
- **Opening a chat from the drawer refetched `/chats`, `/chats/{id}`, and
  Gmail suggested-reminders.** Close-drawer idle-warm hit the list again;
  opening the sidebar also `GET /chats` after titles were already cached;
  route load always `GET` the chat row; composer focus fetched reminders.
  Warm `/chats` only before first paint; skip reopen if the list is loaded;
  reuse the drawer row; composer reads reminder cache only.
- **Learning list open fetched every class detail plus `/home`.** Focus
  refreshed Home and `prefetchProjectDetails` hit each `GET /projects/{id}`.
  Cards only need `GET /projects`; detail loads when a class is opened.
- **Help-me-think / STT still hit `/suggestions` three times.** User bubble
  lands before the socket (`pendingOutboundId`); stream-end flips busy off
  before `refreshKey` bumps — each was a fetch. Hold while turn-busy; fetch
  only on refreshKey or when opening an idle thread. Don't refresh `/home`
  after a chat turn; idle TTS warms clip 0 only.
- **Home open listed the last chat twice (`limit=20`) and POSTed a draft.**
  New chat discarded the routed id, then clearing `chatId` ran the same
  `deleteChatIfEmpty`; warmup also pre-created an empty chat. Discard only
  when the route will not and the thread has no assistant; create on send.
- **Banned chip fields were still copied onto Message.** Backend may send
  `recalled` / `fallback_used` / `context_summarized` for logs; putting them
  on the client message is a second entry point for chips we already removed.
- **Calendar-write blocked Phase B, and calendar-only turns loaded priors.**
  `_load_has_calendar_write` + `_load_prior_user_messages` ran before Tavily/
  Calendar API. Priors only matter when augmenting; write access belongs in
  the integration gather, and only for a create-event hint.
- **Assistant bubbles still wrapped a no-op Show more/less.** `CollapsibleMessageBody`
  with `collapsible={false}` is a passthrough and a second door to fold LLM
  replies. User-message folding stays; assistant body is unwrapped.
- **Learning chats opened Neon to check a quiz letter.** Parse + `is_vocab_quiz_answer`
  only need the already-loaded assistant fence. Open a session only when grading
  a letter answer so ordinary class chat skips that checkout.
- **Composer suggested-reminder chips refetched on every chat focus.** `fetchSuggestedReminders(..., { force: true })` bypassed the 20s cache that Lists already respect. Load without force; invalidate on add/dismiss/Gmail sync still busts.
- **Drawer open, settings tab, and app resume re-hit chat/usage/gallery/home.** Silent
  refetch ignored the 20s stale window home/lists already use. Skip when fresh;
  keep a forced chat pull after backgrounding mid-stream (socket dead, truncated
  bubble). Login must not `force` `/home` twice (token then name).
- **Gallery showed blank tiles (404) after deleting every chat.** Message
  delete SET NULLs `attachments.message_id`, so rows linger after chats/titles
  are gone; chat purge already removed the bytes. List only attachments still
  linked to a message; on local `/file` miss, drop the row. Purge before
  deleting a replaced image-gen assistant so that path does not SET NULL.
- **Every chat turn paid a serial Redis+Neon start plus lookups that cannot apply.**
  Finalize wait ran before user/quota; quiz lookback hit chats with no Learning
  project; prompt assembly re-opened Neon for user/chat already loaded; new chats
  probed attachment chunks; time/location opened a session. Overlap wait with
  user/seed on a *new* message (`gather` finishes before any message read). Do
  not overlap wait with last-message reads — regenerate would race the in-flight
  assistant insert. Skip the rest unless they can apply.
- **Help-me-think home chip took ~6s to first token.** Casual turns still
  loaded the full format/viz/math-solver pack (~4.5k tokens) and ran Gmail
  nudge + web/math/chem prefetch just because they weren't greetings.
  Slim/non-rich turns get the compact math-safety hint; extra prep only
  when `rich_context` or real search/math/chem/calendar/gmail intent.
- **Models invented geometry/graph JSON with fake numbers.** Asking the LLM to
  copy ` ```answer` / ` ```graph` / ` ```geometry` from the hint taught Qwen/GLM
  the JSON protocol, so they emitted fences on unverified turns. Keep those
  fences off the prompt; store them on `canonical_*` and append in
  `validate_math_fences`.
- **Hard physics word problems stayed on DeepSeek Chat, and free Auto threw away smart-chat.** `needs_symbolic` only flags solver-supported templates (digit + drop/projectile/F=ma/energy), so incline/momentum/escape-velocity never escalated. Separately, when Auto wanted `smart-chat` and the free pool had none, `_pick_smart_from_pool` fell through to cheapest (`free-chat`) instead of strongest (`glm-4-flash`). Keep the solver gate on `needs_symbolic`; add a routing-only physics-homework cue; when the preferred tier is missing pick strongest in-pool; sort `chat_fallback_models` by tier proximity to the primary, then price.
- **Learning class detail 500s (`GET /projects/{id}`).** Two bugs stacked: path seed inserts `catalog_entry_id` for words the Python catalog added after the last vocab wipe-migration, so Postgres FK-fails; the handler swallows that, then `expire_all()` + `user.id` lazy-loads in async (`MissingGreenlet`). Snapshot `user_id` before expire; `ensure_catalog_rows()` upserts `vocab_decks`/`vocab_entries` (`ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`) before creating items. Don't wipe-migrate to pick up new words.
- **Live talk `POST /speech/live/speak` 502.** OpenAI `gpt-audio-mini` rejects `audio.format=wav` when `stream=true` (only `pcm16`) and only accepts `wav`/`mp3` input — Expo’s default m4a 400s. Stream pcm16 and wrap WAV; record LINEARPCM wav for live talk (composer mic can stay m4a for Whisper).
- **Physics solver existed but free-fall stayed unverified; KE gained fake height.**
  The pre-stream gate had no physics cues, and a length regex matched `m` inside
  `m/s`. Gate supported templates explicitly; use unit-suffix boundaries and
  bind multiple quantities to their nearest semantic label.
- **Radicals looked like `√` + subscript, and `\sqrt{8^3}` printed a caret.** The
  radical is a row of `[√ Text][radicand View with borderTop]`, so it only holds
  together when both sides share one line box and the bar sits on the ink. Three
  causes stacked: (1) `MathText` fed the radicand to `renderFracSide`, i.e. 11px
  fraction size, then `alignItems: "flex-end"` dropped that short box to the
  baseline; (2) that same helper flattens with `segmentsToPlain`, which turns a
  `sup` segment back into literal `^3`; (3) content kept the base `lineHeight`
  28 while the sign was 20, so the border floated in the leading — 6px above
  both the hook and the digits. Fix: `renderRadicand` renders real segments at
  base size in a tight 20px box (`sqrtSign` / `sqrtBody`), `sqrtRow`
  `flex-start`, nested frac/sqrt keep the flattened View path (a View cannot
  live in that Text); `MathText compact` gives the composer slot the same box.
  Fixing only the composer's `alignItems` (first attempt) left both bugs.
  Related: `\cdot` ate `\cdots` → `·s`; replace `\cdots` / `\ldots` / `\dots`
  before `\cdot`.
- **CI `db_session` ERROR: Future attached to a different loop.** Symptom: `test_chats_db` (or any `*_db.py`) fails in fixture setup, not the test body. Cause: the process-wide async engine still holds asyncpg connections from TestClient/anyio or the previous pytest-asyncio function loop. Dispose-after-test is too late. Fix: `await engine.dispose(close=False)` at the **start** of `db_session` so setup never checks out a foreign-loop connection.
- **Mic stop opened the drawer; New chat then focused the composer.** Parent
  `Gesture.Pan` used view-local `e.x` (~0 on a composer tap) so a mic press
  looked like an edge swipe. Settle could leave the panel on screen with
  `drawerOpen` false → `pointerEvents: none` on the panel, taps hit the
  composer, keyboard opens. Fix: claim with `absoluteX`; keep the panel
  `pointerEvents` auto; no nested `GestureHandlerRootView` in ConversationList.
- **Cloud TTS waited for a full MP3/JSON clip.** `POST /speech/tts` buffered OpenRouter
  `response.content`, wrapped WAV, then `audio_base64`. The app could not start sound until
  the last byte. Fix: `POST /speech/tts/stream` proxies PCM with `aiter_bytes`; mobile plays
  ~120ms WAV clips as they arrive (`ttsPcm.ts`).
- **GitHub “Compare & pull request” on a branch you thought was merged.** Squash-merge
  does not put those SHAs on `main`; pushing more onto the old head (or leaving
  `claude/*` agent branches) recreates a PR prompt. Fix: never push a merged head;
  cherry-pick leftovers onto a new branch from `origin/main`; `git push origin --delete`
  the old branch. See `execution.mdc`.
- **“square root” became a geometry square.** `_extract_square_intent` matched
  substring `"square"` and invented a 5 cm square before algebra/graph
  extractors. Fix: exclude algebraic phrases; default dimensions only with
  draw/show cues (`has_draw_shape`).
- **HTML Run tab solid blank (toolbar ok).** Often not the WebView: HMR left a
  missing symbol (`htmlDependsOnNetwork` / `isWebViewAvailable`); error boundary
  fell back to script-stripped static HTML → white. Also: nav-guard/CSP/onLayout
  stack. Fix: show the real error (no silent static fallback); Run path =
  chart-like `source={{ html }}` only + `prepareHtmlRunDocument` (live CSP +
  in-document stay script); clear Metro cache after preview edits.
- **“No internet” banner stuck after Wi‑Fi returns.** Cause: NetInfo
  `isConnected`/`isInternetReachable` can stay stale and `NetInfo.refresh()` can
  remain unresolved; 1.5s polling also overlapped slower probes. Fix: bound the
  refresh, race API + public generate_204 checks, and keep offline polling
  single-flight; online NetInfo still clears immediately.
- **Login “Rate limit unavailable” / auth 429 with API healthy.** Cause: Upstash free tier
  hit max-requests; REST limiter fails closed on any Redis error, and token issue needs Redis
  too. Fix: point local `REDIS_URL` at Homebrew Redis (`redis://127.0.0.1:6379`); keep Upstash
  for prod. Expo `react` must stay on SDK pin (`19.2.3` for Expo 57) — Dependabot patch bumps
  break Hermes boot with `property is not writable`.
- **CO₂ diagram looked like O₂.** Cause: smiles-drawer skeletal mode hides chain carbons
  (`O=C=O` → only “O=O” labels). Fix: after `processGraph`, set `drawExplicit` on every C
  before `drawVertices`.
- **Chemistry SMILES WebView: “Could not render that structure.”** Cause: smiles-drawer
  2.1.7 `Drawer.draw(..., infoOnly)` forwards `infoOnly` as `SvgDrawer`’s `weights`, so
  `false.every` throws (caught as parse/draw failure). Fix: use `SvgDrawer` on an `<svg>`
  and call `draw(tree, el, theme)` with no 4th arg.
- **Image-gen sheet came back after “composer only”.** Cause: attach row was removed but
  `useChatSend` still opened `ImageGenPromptSheet` on intent. Fix: delete the sheet + call
  `submitPrompt` on send. Rule: replace UX → delete old path (chat-ux-bans).
- **Raw `(\frac{...})` inline math on screen.** Model `\(...\)` survived preprocess, then
  CommonMark escaped `\(`/`\)` to bare parens before `splitInlineMath` — MathText never
  ran. Also `looksLikeProseParenthetical` counted `\neq`/`\frac` letter-runs as English.
  Fix (#450): convert `\(...\)` → `$...$` in `protectMathEscapes`; strip `\\[a-zA-Z]+`
  before the prose-word count; wrap bare cmds outside existing `$` spans.
- **Chat “falls then snaps back” when stream ends.** ChatGPT drops copy/thumbs
  into the empty space above the composer; the prose does not move. Recall
  reserved that height both as list pad and as an in-bubble slot, and native
  autoscroll + JS `scrollToEnd` + a leftover streaming catch-up all wrote at
  the 280ms settle — spring, and the scroll-to-bottom chevron appeared. Fix:
  pad = composer gap only while the last row is the `streaming` placeholder;
  mount icons when that row persists (same render, net zero); cancel streaming
  scroll on end; keep native autoscroll off until `STREAM_AUTOSCROLL_RESUME_MS`.
- **Streaming math boxes flicker (blank → repaint).** Pending stream tail re-parsed
  every flush; `react-native-markdown-display` re-keys the tree so KaTeX WebViews in that
  tail remount. Short closed ` ```math ` / `$$` blocks sat under the 320-char settle
  threshold for many flushes. Fix (#443): `advanceStreamBlocks` eagerly cuts at the next
  safe blank line once a fence/`$$` has closed — don’t wait on char volume.
- **Chat cold start pulled Mermaid/Vega/MathJax.** Static imports from `RichFence` /
  `mathHtml` evaluated ~6MB of inlined vendors on every markdown message graph load.
  Fix: `React.lazy` Chart/Mermaid via `LazyHeavyRich`; MathJax in `mathHtmlMathjax`
  loaded only for multline/eqnarray when a WebView can mount.
- **Drawer menu needs many taps after Reanimated migrate.** Opaque left-edge hit strip
  (`zIndex` 210) sat on the hamburger; failed pan `onFinalize` also raced `settle(false)`
  against `open()`. Fix: `manualActivation` (claim only after horizontal move) + settle
  cancel only if the pan actually activated.
- **RNSVG “Codegen didn't run” flood.** Metro `resolveRequest` used Node `require.resolve('react-native-svg')` → `lib/commonjs`, skipping package.json `"react-native": "src/"`. Fabric babel codegen never ran. Dedupe via Metro's resolver with a pinned `originModulePath` instead.
- **Model toggles snap back mid-flip.** Controlled Switch waited on Auth context; racing
  bootstrap `updateMe({timezone|location}).then(setUser)` replaced the whole user with
  stale `enabled_models`. Fix: local draft prefs; `updateUser` generation guard; bootstrap
  merges only patched fields (`useBootstrapSync`).
- **Memory screen always waits on network.** Settings already `GET /memories` for the count,
  then `/memory` refetched from empty. Fix: shared `memoryListCache` (20s TTL + inflight
  dedupe); prefetch on Settings→Memory; hydrate on mount; invalidate on logout.
- **Header actions flicker while a chat is open.** `hasMessages={messages.length > 0}` drops
  the action group if the list briefly clears during load/refetch. Gate on
  `messages.length > 0 || routeChatId` so an active chat route keeps controls mounted.
- **iOS Simulator soft keyboard missing.** Host Connect Hardware Keyboard hides it.
  `defaults write com.apple.iphonesimulator ConnectHardwareKeyboard -bool false` (+ device
  prefs) and relaunch; ⌘K if needed. osascript cannot toggle Simulator without Accessibility.
- **TTS 502 ≠ API down.** OpenRouter has no OpenAI GPT TTS (`gpt-4o-mini-tts*` 400
  “does not exist”). Use a listed speech model such as
  `google/gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview` (PCM only — wrap as WAV). `/speech/tts` 502
  while the rest of the API stays healthy is a model-id / format bug, not an outage.
- **WS ASGI Traceback on navigate.** `WebSocketDisconnect(1000)` while `chat_websocket` waits
  for auth JSON = client closed mid-reconnect; noisy, not a fatal server failure.
- **Image goes blurry/gray after the assistant replies.** Focus refetch after `streaming→false` replaces `local-*` ids with server UUIDs; id-only `mergeLocalAttachmentUris` dropped `local_image_uri` and restarted blur reveal. Also match orphaned local URIs onto incoming user attachment messages; user thumbs use `animatedReveal={false}`.
- **Attachment send showed `[BEGIN UNTRUSTED…]` + blurry spinner.** `wrap_untrusted` was persisted into the user message; focus refetch then dropped `local_image_uri` so ChatMessageImage remounted on a remote auth URL. Persist plain `[Image:]`/`[File:]` only; merge local URIs on refetch; skip blur reveal for `file://`.
- **CodeQL poly-ReDoS not cleared by `collapse_ws` / length caps.** CodeQL ignores those as sanitizers; rewrite sinks to linear scans (`find` / digit parse). See `.cursor/skills/security-alert-pitfalls/SKILL.md`.
- **Dependabot on transitive npm (markdown-it@10, uuid@7).** Direct pins don't help — use `pnpm.overrides` + regenerate lock with `npx pnpm@9.15.9 install`. See security-alert-pitfalls skill.
- **Raw LaTeX + smashed prose in math bubbles.** `normalizeImplicitMath` re-wrapped `(excluded values: $x …$)` / `(e.g., … like $x^4$)` as `$…$$`, inventing a trailing `$$` that stole the next display-math opener — equations showed raw and Wait—prose became a MathBlock (italic, no spaces). Fix: skip parens that already contain `$` or look like English prose (2+ letter-words).
- **SecureStore Keychain “required entitlement isn’t present” on simulator.** Linker-signed/adhoc builds (`TeamIdentifier=not set`, no identities) get `errSecMissingEntitlement` (-34018) on `setItemAsync`. Don’t put non-secrets (list order) in SecureStore — use filesystem; catch SecureStore writes. Proper Keychain needs a local Apple signing identity + `expo run:ios` rebuild.
- **Quiz wrong-answer UX: hint only, no re-render.** User rejected re-asking the same MCQ
  after a miss. Prompts must not emit a new ```vocab_quiz on wrong; chips stay on the prior
  quiz message (`findActiveQuizMessageId`). Grade against `get_last_quiz_assistant`, not the
  hint-only last assistant.
- **Quiz answers “don’t register” (Today stays 0/x).** Causes: (1) nested `session.commit()` in
  `messages.create` / `apply_quiz_result` mid–turn_prep; (2) letter answer + missing `vocab_quiz`
  fence → grade `None` and `skip_memory_jobs` blocked background sync; (3) My Learning 20s stale
  cache. Fix: `commit=False` until one outer commit; don’t skip jobs when letter grade fails;
  force-refresh projects list/detail on focus; invalidate home after grade.
- **Unpushed local diffs cause real pain.** User runs other machines/simulators off `main` /
  remote — finish every change with commit + push (see `execution.mdc`); don't say done with
  local-only work.
- **User rejected “Recalled N memories” chip + assistant Show more/less.** Do not reintroduce —
  see `.cursor/rules/chat-ux-bans.mdc`. Code-block fold only; assistant body stays unfolded.
- **User rejected model-fallback / context-summarized chips** (`chat.model_fallback` raw key
  flashed in chat). Do not reintroduce — see chat-ux-bans §4.
- **`ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH` on patchedDependencies.** Regenerating `pnpm-lock.yaml`
  with pnpm 11 drops patch metadata while `package.json` still declares patches; CI uses pnpm 9 and
  fails frozen install. Regenerate with `npx pnpm@9.15.9 install` (or pin `"packageManager"`).
- **Simulator can't reach LAN API URL.** Physical device needs `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<lan-ip>:8000`
  (`./scripts/set-lan-ip.sh`); iOS Simulator needs `http://127.0.0.1:8000` (`./scripts/set-sim-ip.sh`
  or `./scripts/dev.sh mobile-sim`). Wrong URL → login/chat fails with network errors, not a code bug.
- **"Coverage is failing" but really lint/types are.** CI order is `ruff check → ruff format
  --check → mypy → pytest --cov-fail-under=80`; an earlier step failing means pytest never runs.
  Run the whole chain locally before committing, not just pytest.
- **Unpinned dev tooling silently breaks CI.** `mypy`/`ruff` were `>=`, so CI pulled a newer,
  stricter mypy and failed. Keep them capped in `pyproject.toml` and pin Python (`<3.14`).
- **SQLAlchemy `.rowcount` fails mypy.** `await session.execute(delete(...))` is typed `Result`
  (no `.rowcount`) → `cast(CursorResult[Any], await session.execute(...))`. Also never
  `from sqlalchemy import update` in a repo that defines its own `update()` (F811 shadow → wrong
  symbol at type-check).
- **mypy won't narrow a doubled `.get()`.** `usage.get("x") if usage.get("x") is not None else …`
  stays `int | None`. Assign to a local first, then branch on the local.
- **HTML/JS WebView preview "not working" = wrong build, not a bug.** `react-native-webview` is a
  native module; it never works in Expo Go. Rebuild the dev client (`pnpm expo run:ios`). It
  falls back to static HTML (scripts stripped) otherwise.
- **System dark mode on a static `C` palette.** Keep `C` (light) for unmigrated screens; add
  `useTheme()` and convert module-level `StyleSheet.create` into `makeX(t: Theme)` factories
  called via `useMemo`. Low-churn and incremental.
- **Mobile deps won't install in this env.** npm points at an auth-gated internal registry, so
  `tsc`/Expo can't run here — verify mobile changes with `pnpm typecheck`/`pnpm lint` locally.
- **expo-av / voice crash (`ExponentAV` not found).** `expo-av` is incompatible with SDK 56 — use
  `expo-audio` instead; lazy-load via `lib/voiceAudio.ts` for Expo Go; rebuild dev client with
  `pnpm expo run:ios` (not Expo Go).
